      "message": "Since all external callers are being migrated to the static factory methods, consider moving the constructors and two-stage initialization methods (`Attach`, `Create`, etc.) to the `private:` section to enforce the new initialization pattern.\n\nNote that if you make the constructors private, `std::make_unique\u003cCFX_RenderDevice\u003e(...)` inside the factory methods will fail to compile. You can work around this by using direct allocation, e.g., `pdfium::WrapUnique(new CFX_RenderDevice())` (or `absl::WrapUnique`).",
